<h1>1. Project Overview</h1>
<h2>Purpose of the Website</h2>
<p>
  Accbot is a premium web portal designed for businesses operating in Dubai and the wider UAE. It provides high-end accounting, VAT advisory, tax filing, corporate bookkeeping, and company formation services. In addition to marketing services, the portal offers integrated tools like an <strong>Expense Tracker</strong> and <strong>Accounts Web</strong> dashboard to help registered clients manage corporate receipts, track compliance parameters, and review ledger structures in real-time.
</p>
<h2>Main Features</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Services Exploration & Detailed Pages:</strong> Interactive pages describing FTA-compliant auditing, bookkeeping, VAT management, and company registration.</li>
  <li><strong>Authentication & Security:</strong> Robust email/password signup and login, integrated with Google OAuth 2.0 Sign-In, secured by custom JWT (JSON Web Tokens) stored in HttpOnly, Secure cookies.</li>
  <li><strong>User Profile Settings:</strong> Centralized dashboard for clients to manage contact details and profiles.</li>
  <li><strong>Expense Tracker & Accounts Web:</strong> Integrated utility platforms allowing corporate users to keep records of financial operations.</li>
  <li><strong>Administrative Control Panel:</strong> Complete admin interface for staff to inspect website metrics, handle contact inquiry messages, configure settings, and monitor user accounts.</li>
  <li><strong>Activity Logging:</strong> Audit logs tracking critical modifications, roles, and administrative interventions.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Overall Workflow</h2>
<p>
  A guest user visits the homepage, browsing UAE compliance articles, services, and testimonials. They submit contact requests, which are recorded in the database. When they register an account, an entry is created in Supabase Auth and a database trigger immediately provisions a corresponding client profile in the public database. Upon logging in, the user receives HttpOnly JWT cookies representing their active session. They can update profile information and browse client modules (Expense Tracker, Accounts Web). Administrative roles can access guarded routes under <code>/admin</code> to audit messages, logs, and services.
</p>

<h1>2. Current Progress</h1>
<h2>What Has Been Completed So Far</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Technical Core:</strong> Configured Next.js 16 App Router environment with TypeScript and Tailwind CSS v4 styling systems.</li>
  <li><strong>Custom JWT Authentication Utility:</strong> Written <code>src/lib/jwt.ts</code> wrapping the <code>jose</code> library to securely sign and verify access tokens (15m expiry) and refresh tokens (7d/30d expiry) using a secure 256-bit key.</li>
  <li><strong>Cookie Management:</strong> Formulated <code>src/lib/auth-cookies.ts</code> to configure secure cookie parameters (HttpOnly, Lax, Secure) to protect user credentials against Cross-Site Scripting (XSS) and Cross-Site Request Forgery (CSRF).</li>
  <li><strong>Auth API Endpoint Implementations:</strong> Deployed <code>GET /api/auth/token</code> (exchanging Supabase sessions for JWTs), <code>POST /api/auth/refresh</code> (handling silent token rotation), and <code>POST /api/auth/signout</code> (clearing cookies).</li>
  <li><strong>Google Sign-In Integration:</strong> Integrated Google OAuth 2.0 client redirection and callback handling in <code>src/actions/auth.ts</code> and <code>src/app/auth/callback/route.ts</code> to support Google Identity logins.</li>
  <li><strong>Protected Middleware:</strong> Configured <code>src/middleware.ts</code> to inspect session statuses, invoke JWT decoders, and handle access redirection for all protected application routes.</li>
  <li><strong>Database Schemas & Tables:</strong> Configured complete schema file (<code>supabase/schema.sql</code>) containing specifications for profiles, settings, services, logs, and refresh token tables.</li>
  <li><strong>Admin Portal Layout & Interface:</strong> Implemented admin layouts with sections for user reviews, incoming messages, and administrative parameters.</li>
</ul>

