<h1>4. Technology Stack</h1>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Frontend:</strong> Next.js 16 (App Router structure), React 19, TypeScript for static typing, Tailwind CSS v4 for UI layouts, Framer Motion for micro-animations, Lucide React for consistent vector symbols, Shadcn UI (radix primitives) for accessible components.</li>
  <li><strong>Backend:</strong> Next.js Server Actions (secures mutations without explicit API boilerplate), Next.js Route Handlers (REST api routing for auth tokens and signouts).</li>
  <li><strong>Database & Real-time:</strong> Supabase PostgreSQL. RLS (Row-Level Security) acts as the data firewall, filtering queries based on user context. Database triggers automate public profiles synchronization.</li>
  <li><strong>Authentication:</strong> Custom JWT tokens (using HS256 algorithm via <code>jose</code>) stored as secure, HttpOnly cookies for protection against token theft. Google Cloud OAuth 2.0 integration via Google Identity APIs.</li>
  <li><strong>Hosting & Server Architecture:</strong> Hosted on Railway. Environment variable vault holds all database links and secret keys.</li>
</ul>

<h1>5. Project Architecture</h1>
<h2>High-Level Architecture</h2>
<div class="diagram-box">
+-------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|                              User Browser                               |
