<h1>7. Database Design</h1>
<h2>PostgreSQL Schema Description</h2>
<p>
  The database is hosted on Supabase (PostgreSQL). It contains nine main tables. Row-Level Security (RLS) is enabled on all tables, preventing unauthorized manipulation.
</p>

<h3>Database Tables Schema Reference</h3>
<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th>Table Name</th>
      <th>Primary Key</th>
      <th>Relationships / Foreign Keys</th>
      <th>Description</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td><code>public.profiles</code></td>
      <td><code>id (uuid)</code></td>
      <td>References <code>auth.users(id)</code></td>
      <td>Stores user profiles. Synchronized automatically via database triggers on registrations.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><code>public.contact_messages</code></td>
      <td><code>id (uuid)</code></td>
      <td>None</td>
      <td>Contains user contact inquiry details.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><code>public.services</code></td>
      <td><code>id (uuid)</code></td>
      <td>None</td>
      <td>Details of services offered (Audit, VAT, Bookkeeping, etc.).</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><code>public.testimonials</code></td>
      <td><code>id (uuid)</code></td>
      <td>None</td>
